@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .gitignore@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": .smysl/extractions/ }
~ Track `.smysl/extractions/` directory

To ensure that the raw model answers behind each record are tracked, making D7's 'extract once per commit and recipe' true across clones.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/b2dbe4820872.json@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "cargo-smysl-facts = { workspace = true }" }
~ Add `cargo-smysl-facts` as a dependency

To support the retrieval and matching of facts, which is part of the verdict stage.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/b2dbe4820872.json@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": pub mod matching; }
~ Add `matching` module to `lib.rs`

To handle the checking of one claim against the facts, as part of the matching process.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-4 { status: speculative, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "[dependencies]\ncargo-smysl-facts = { workspace = true }\n\n[features]\ndefault = []\n# Hosted providers need TLS; the default build has no network stack at all, which is what the self-contained objective and the CI rule mean (D18).\nhosted = [\"cargo-smysl-extract/hosted\"]" }
~ Update `Cargo.toml` with new dependencies and features

To include necessary crates for the new functionality and to define features like `hosted` that require TLS.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-5 { status: speculative, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "/// Check a recorded claim against the code, and say what may be concluded (D11, D12).\nEvidence { .. } => not_yet(\"evidence\", \"Phase 3 — verdicts and test evidence\")," }
~ Add `Evidence` command to `cli.rs`

To allow checking a recorded claim against the code and saying what may be concluded, as part of Phase 3.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/b2dbe4820872.json@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "pub fn retrieve<'a>(claim: &str, facts: &'a [Fact], r: &Retrieval) -> Shown<'a> {" }
~ Add `retrieve` function to `matching.rs`

To retrieve the facts worth showing for one claim based on the overlap with the claim's terms.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-7 { status: speculative, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "pub fn match_claim(\n    claim: &str,\n    shown: &Shown<'_>,\n    judge: &dyn Judge,\n    r: &Retrieval,\n) -> Result<Matched, JudgeError> {" }
~ Add `match_claim` function to `matching.rs`

To ask about one claim and validate the citations provided by the model.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/b2dbe4820872.json@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "pub const SYSTEM: &str = \"You check one claim about a Rust codebase against facts taken from the code.\\n...\"" }
~ Add `SYSTEM` constant to `matching.rs`

To define the system prompt for the model when checking one claim against facts.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/extractions/v1/b2dbe4820872.json@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "[derive(Debug, Default, Deserialize)]\nstruct Answer {" }
~ Add `Answer` struct to `matching.rs`

To represent the JSON answer provided by the model after checking a claim.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-10 { status: speculative, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "[derive(Debug, Clone)]\npub struct Matched {" }
~ Add `Matched` struct to `matching.rs`

To represent the result of matching a claim against the shown facts, including any invented citations.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-11 { status: speculative, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "/// Checking one claim against facts (D11): what is retrieved, what is asked, and what a citation must be.\n\nuse std::cell::RefCell;\n\nuse cargo_smysl_extract::{Charged, Judge, JudgeError};\nuse cargo_smysl_facts::facts;\nuse cargo_smysl_verdict::matching::{match_claim, retrieve, Retrieval};\nuse cargo_smysl_verdict::policy::{decide, Verdict};" }
~ Add tests for `matching.rs`

To ensure that the retrieval and matching of claims against facts works as expected.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:b17287cebb93435d50f195ca0c15ef0c72eeff5c }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Track the extraction cache: a clone without it pays 7 to 30 minutes a commit }
~ Track the extraction cache: a clone without it pays 7 to 30 minutes a commit

The raw model answers behind each record are not derived — a model is not deterministic, so re-running does not reproduce them — and they are what makes D7's 'extract once per commit and recipe' true across clones rather than only on the machine that did it.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-13 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The tool assigns sources, labels and statuses; a model proposes content only." }
~ The tool assigns sources, labels and statuses; a model proposes content only

The tool promises that each command does what its design says, with measured figures where a model is involved (recall, precision, cost). Acting on its reports belongs to whoever reads them: a person, a CI step, a hook, an agent.

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-14 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Extraction is multi-pass with the diff: decisions first, then prerequisites / alternatives / consequences in parallel. A pro-class model for prerequisites at minimum" }
~ Extraction is multi-pass with the diff: decisions first, then prerequisites / alternatives / consequences in …

Flash-lite ~30% genuine prerequisites vs pro ~75%

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-15 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Extract once per commit; improvements arrive as 'supersedes', never as re-extraction merged into the store" }
~ Extract once per commit; improvements arrive as 'supersedes', never as re-extraction merged into the store

Stability experiment

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-16 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Quotes are checked against the message and diff with quote_support_in; an absent quote caps the unit at 'speculative' }
~ Quotes are checked against the message and diff with quote_support_in; an absent quote caps the unit at …

0 of 138 absent quotes with pro; fabricated alternatives caught with flash-lite

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-17 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Facts are deterministic and live in a regenerable cache, not the corpus. Scope: items the diff touches, code identifiers named in the message or prerequisite, one call hop outward, reverse 'called by' edges, manifest / CI-matrix / git facts" }
~ Facts are deterministic and live in a regenerable cache, not the corpus

~7 MB of facts per commit; rounds 1–6

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-18 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Author text is prose and never verifies: }
~ Author text is prose and never verifies

rounds 3–6: every one of these laundered support until tagged

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-19 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Fact matching retrieves per prerequisite (BM25 plus neighbours plus named items, 30 structural + 10 prose facts), and the model judges one claim at a time" }
~ Fact matching retrieves per prerequisite (BM25 plus neighbours plus named items, 30 structural + 10 prose …

round 5: 16 correct, 0 false contradictions

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-20 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Verdict policy: a single run never raises a status. SUPPORTED requires model coverage 'full' and every part covered by a structural fact, and two independent runs agreeing (or a person). PARTIAL / PROSE_ONLY / IMPLEMENTED_BY attach evidence only; CONTRADICTED goes to review" }
~ Verdict policy: a single run never raises a status. SUPPORTED requires model coverage 'full' and every part …

round 6: part-based coverage alone overclaimed 4 times; two-run agreement had 1 wrong of 7

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-21 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Test evidence: link tests to prerequisites (verifies / exercises / unrelated), run each at the commit with --locked, the features its cfg requires, and --exact; import results with from_csv as measured data units; backs / rebuts for verifies, x.code/exercises for exercises. Prerequisite statuses never change from test results alone" }
~ Test evidence: link tests to prerequisites (verifies / exercises / unrelated), run each at the commit with …

test-evidence run: 53 tests, 50 passed, attested stores; S1: 3 of 17 'verifies' links wrong, 1 vacuous test

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-22 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The model is the operator's choice, never the tool's." }
~ The model is the operator's choice, never the tool's

Provider (ollama, any OpenAI-compatible endpoint), model, endpoint, key variable, context window and the system prompt come from flags, the environment or configuration, with sensible defaults and the prompt tunable per provider; a run records which it used. The default is local (Ollama), so the tool costs nothing to try

@decision d/gb17287cebb93-23 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: docs/implementation-plan.md@b17287cebb93 }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The model client is our own, and the default build has no network stack." }
~ The model client is our own, and the default build has no network stack

`check` speaks plain HTTP/1.1 to a local provider (Ollama, or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint on `http://`), written out rather than pulled in; a hosted provider over TLS is the `hosted` feature, off by default. This settles item 7: smysl's `model` feature would bring `smysl-provider` and a TLS stack into every install, and the multi-pass schemas do not fit `PromptOverride` anyway. `check` ships advisory — findings print, the exit code stays 0 unless `--strict`, which exits 5

